    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d400">

                <pb facs="0561" n="455" sameAs="frus:frus1891/pg455"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Pung to Mr. Blaine</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Chinese Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1891-03-09"><hi rendition="#italic">March 9,
                        1891</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to bring to your kind
                    notice the gratifying announcement of the following cablegram from the foreign
                    office in Peking, received yesterday: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>All the ministers had an audience on the 25th day of the present month
                            (March 5th, instant), and were banqueted on the following day (March 6,
                            instant). Appropriate ceremonies were most pleasantly observed on both
                            occasions. Please communicate the above to the honorable Secretary of
                            State of the United States.</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Pung Kwang Yu</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
